    "title": "Linux Shell",
    "description": "As part of my Introduction to Systems Programming course (CS 3560), I built a simple Linux shell which reads strings from the user and executes the specified commands. It supports command line arguments, Pipelines, I/O Redirection and forking.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jun 2016 - Sep 2016"
   },
   {
    "title": "Pacman Game",
    "description": "As part of the Software Engineering 1 (CS 4310) course, we built a terminal based ASCII Pacman game. We developed it in C for Unix/Linux operating system and we used libraries ncurses and pthread. I implemented the movement of the 'Monsters' (Or 'Ghosts') in a separate thread than the main game thread using the pthread library.",
